# Trivy misconfiguration baseline for `infrastructure/` (scan-type: config).
#
# Two sections:
#   1. ACCEPTED   — deliberate architectural decisions. Not going to change.
#   2. TECH-DEBT  — real findings, baselined so the scanner can go live green.
#                   Fix the underlying issue, then delete the line so any
#                   regression is caught again.
#
# Anything NOT listed here fails the build (CRITICAL/HIGH). Add new entries
# only with a justification comment.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. ACCEPTED — architectural decisions
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# S3 buckets use SSE-S3 (AES256), not a customer-managed KMS key. Chosen
# deliberately for these buckets (assets/logs/state); CMK is not required.
# See modules/s3, modules/metastore-s3, modules/cloudtrail.
AVD-AWS-0132

# CloudTrail log objects inherit the same SSE-S3 choice as above (no CMK).
AVD-AWS-0015

# The application ALB is intentionally internet-facing — it is the public
# entrypoint for the web/API. Access is controlled by SGs + WAF, not privacy.
AVD-AWS-0053

# Public subnets auto-assign public IPs by design (they host the ALB / NAT).
# Workloads run in private subnets. See modules/vpc.
AVD-AWS-0164

# Default-open egress (0.0.0.0/0) is accepted for these security groups;
# egress is not the control boundary here. See modules/vpc.
AVD-AWS-0104
